#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059490 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1938c5da-d01a-53b7-a811-9afe1e43d152" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Entries of a Matrix Product Representing a 3x3 System of Equations"}] :question/id #uuid "7bfcfcbb-6212-5f9b-90aa-c79fbf7221e9" :question/math-academy-id "e-4518" :question/problem "The system of equations\n${6x + 4y = 1; x - 8y - z =-2; 3x + 2y - 2z = 1$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$\\begin{bmatrix}a & 4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -8 & -1 \\\\ 3 & b & -2\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nWhat are the values of $a$, $b$ and $c$?" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n{6x + 4y + 0z = 1; x - 8y - z =-2; 3x + 2y - 2z = 1\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form\n\n$$\nA\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -8 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation\n\n$$\nA\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}\n$$\n\nbecomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -8 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=6$, $b=2$, and $c=-2$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059491 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7958ef60-8041-535b-bff8-b35e84c54412" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Entries of a Matrix Product Representing a 3x3 System of Equations by Reorganizing"}] :question/id #uuid "c4af8b0d-e4ee-56f4-9cf6-594530639339" :question/math-academy-id "e-4519" :question/problem "The system of equations\n${2x - y + z = 4; z - x + 2 =-1; 2y - 2x - 4z =-4$\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n$\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & a & 1 \\\\ b & 2 & -4\\end{bmatrix}$\nWhat are the values of $a$, $b$ and $c$?" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n{2x - y + z = 4; - x + 0y + z =-3; - 2x + 2y - 4z =-4\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form\n\n$$\nA\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation\n\n$$\nA\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}\n$$\n\nbecomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore $a=0$, $b=-2$, $c=-3$."}]}
